# Data conversion between mebibyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between mebibyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MiB to 0.0000TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 0.0000TB; backward, converting 1TB to 953674.3164MiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TB yields 1430511.4746MiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(MiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(MiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TB
0.0000TB
953674.3164MiB
1430511.4746MiB

<<< stderr
